analysisWe need to produce a single assert statement reflecting the comment.

We have a class AttributeList extends ArrayList<Object>. Method add(Attribute attribute) adds attribute via super.add(attribute). Then comment: "If the attribute is null, then the last element in the list is also null; if the attribute is not null, then it equals the last element in the list."

We need to refer to list methods: size(), get(int). Since we are inside this class, we can use this.get(int) and this.size(). The last element index is this.size() - 1 after addition.

We need to capture both cases: attribute == null => this.get(this.size()-1) == null; attribute != null => this.get(this.size()-1).equals(attribute) (or == attribute? Since they are objects, we can use .equals). Use attribute variable.

Thus assert: (attribute == null => this.get(this.size()-1) == null) && (attribute != null => this.get(this.size()-1).equals(attribute));

Make sure syntax: attribute == null => this.get(this.size()-1) == null

Combine with &&.

Thus final answer:

<code>assert (attribute == null => this.get(this.size()-1) == null) && (attribute != null => this.get(this.size()-1).equals(attribute));</code>

